      "status": "ok",
      "summary": "Decision preview is BLOCK and should remain BLOCK. The candidate change sets Deployment/demo/demo env[6] to DEMO_STARTUP_FAIL=true, which the FAULT_INJECTION rule flags as a deliberate startup failure. Trusted cases confirm this env value is a drill fault, not a shippable setting: the new Pod would log startup_failed and enter CrashLoop while the old Pod keeps serving, so this validates rollout protection rather than a healthy release. Do not treat old-Pod readiness as release success. Additional review concerns: 35 scheduled Pods lack CPU/memory requests so free capacity may be overstated; KubeCPUOvercommit is firing; request_rate is 0, so zero errors/latency cannot be read as healthy. The AI result status is invalid (ERROR). Remediation must go through a Git revert commit and Argo resync, not an imperative rollback."
    },
